3112..3187 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every word: the round trip at a variable, by"
3188..3262 Comment "/// induction over the presented words. The result type reads the word the"
3263..3334 Comment "/// fold descends on, so each arm answers it at its constructor and the"
3335..3393 Comment "/// recursive call at the field: `sectWords[<](x)` relates"
3394..3469 Comment "/// `spinWords(windWords(x))` to `x`, and carried along `around` it relates"
3470..3544 Comment "/// `Loop(spinWords(windWords(x)))`, which `spinWords(windWords(Loop(x)))`"
3545..3622 Comment "/// runs to, to `Loop(x)`. The case respects both rules: at `Loop(Unloop(x))`"
3623..3697 Comment "/// the arms compose to `cong(around, cong(unaround, p))`, whose functions"
3698..3774 Comment "/// compose to the identity under the rules, so the chain is `p` itself, the"
3775..3793 Comment "/// answer at `x`."
